+
+## Requirement (Pillar 1 — Adapt the requirement)
+
+User report: `python3 -m tally add 18.40 eating-out "pho, then bubble tea"` prints "Added", but afterwards `tally list` and `tally summary` fail with `error: ... expected 4 fields, got 5`. "Notes with commas in them should just work."
+
+**Restated intent**: A note may contain commas (and quotes). It is saved so that it reads back unchanged, and `list` / `summary` keep working.
+
+**Root cause (Supervisor finding)**: `src/tally/storage.py` reads with `csv.reader` but writes with a naive `",".join(expense.to_row())` in `append` (line 53) and `save_all` (line 61). The writer does not quote fields.
+
+**Out of scope**:
+- Repairing already-corrupt lines in `data/expenses.csv` (the user removed theirs by hand).
+- Newlines in notes (still rejected by `Expense.__post_init__`).
+- `src/tally/recurring.py` (it only reads, via `csv.DictReader`).
+
+**Requirement Refs**: None (no `PRD.md` in this repo).
+
+### Requirement Fidelity Gate (sign off BEFORE implementation)
+
+- [x] Restated intent confirmed to match the user's request
+- [x] Domain terms align (no glossary exists)
+- [x] Every Acceptance Criterion below traces to a line in the Requirement
+- [x] Requirement Refs: none apply
+
+---
+
+## Dependencies & Reachability
+
+**Depends on**: `None`
+
+**Entry point**: `storage.append`
+
+---
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+| # | Criterion (testable) | Traces to requirement |
+|---|----------------------|-----------------------|
+| 1 | An expense whose note contains a comma, written with `storage.append`, loads back equal to the original | "notes with commas should just work" |
+| 2 | Same round-trip through `storage.save_all` | same (delete path rewrites the file) |
+| 3 | A note with a double quote and a comma round-trips | boundary |
+| 4 | Plain notes still write unquoted, so existing files and `HEADER` are unchanged | no regression |
+| 5 | CLI: `add ... "pho, then bubble tea"` then `list` and `summary` succeed | the reported failure |
+
+---
+
+## Evaluation & Acceptance
+
+### Success Criteria
+
+| # | Given | Expect | How it's checked |
+|---|-------|--------|------------------|
+| 1 | `Expense(..., note="pho, then bubble tea")` appended | `load()` returns an equal Expense | automated test |
+| 2 | Note `say "hi", ok` | round-trips | automated test |
+| 3 | CLI add with comma note, then list | exit 0, note shown | automated test in `tests/test_cli.py` |
+
